================================================================================
Astronomy Engine — astronomy.kt
================================================================================
Source:    https://github.com/cosinekitty/astronomy
Author:    Don Cross <cosinekitty@gmail.com>
License:   MIT
Bundled:   Yes — vendored source file at
           core/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/fritze/skyward/core/astro/vendored/astronomy.kt
Notes:     Copyright and license header retained in the vendored file, per the
           MIT license's attribution requirement. Not fetched from JitPack;
           the upstream Kotlin/JVM artifact is JVM-only, but the source file
           itself is pure Kotlin and compiles unmodified in commonMain.

================================================================================
Stellarium meteor-shower catalog — showers.json
================================================================================
Source:    https://github.com/Stellarium/stellarium
           (plugins/MeteorShowers/resources/MeteorShowers.json, renamed here)
License:   GPL-2.0-or-later
Bundled:   Yes — as a :core resource (core/src/commonMain/resources/showers.json,
           duplicated at core/src/androidMain/resources/showers.json — see the
           comment in ShowersResource.android.kt for why)
Notes:     Meteor shower data from the Stellarium project. This dependency is
           why Skyward is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later (D8) — GPLv3+ is
           compatible with GPL-2.0-or-later, so bundling is permitted. Field
           semantics (activity start/finish/peak are solar-longitude degrees,
           not calendar dates; drift is applied per degree of solar longitude
           travelled, not per day) were verified against the plugin's own
           C++ source, not assumed — see docs/adr/0003-shower-solar-longitude.md.

